{
  "slug": "ccguard",
  "name": "Ccguard",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Security guard hook for Claude Code. Evaluates every tool call (Bash, Edit, Write, Read, MCP) against 864 pattern-matching rules to block dangerous commands, data exfiltration, and supply chain attacks. Zero external dependencies, written in Zig. Supports three decision levels: allow, deny (hard block), and ask (user confirmation prompt). Protects against reverse shells, pipe-to-interpreter execution, credential leakage, cloud metadata access, environment variable injection, and more.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **2 hooks**, `SessionStart`, `PreToolUse`.\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install ccguard@claude-community` from `soyukke/ccguard`.\n\nA security guard written in Zig that stops Claude Code before it runs `rm -rf /`.\n\nSecurity guard hook for Claude Code. Evaluates every tool call (Bash, Edit, Write, Read, MCP) against 864 pattern-matching rules to block dangerous commands, data exfiltration, and supply chain attacks. Zero external dependencies, written in Zig. Supports three decision levels: allow, deny (hard block), and ask (user confirmation prompt). Protects against reverse shells, pipe-to-interpreter execution, credential leakage, cloud metadata access, environment variable injection, and more.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "hook",
  "sourceType": "community",
